        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Euphorbia grandidens, commonly known as valleybush euphorbia or large-toothed euphorbia, is a species of plant in the family Euphorbiaceae native to southern Africa. While sometimes shrubby, it can also be a pachycaulous tree up to {{convert|15|m}} tall, with the short horizontal branches in a rosette at the top of the main trunk and reiterations. These horizontal branches are succulent and triangular in cross-section."
          }
